{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cet8RwpN4DYwkDzqqDhBP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! The baseline tests all pass. Now I have my complete analysis ready to move to the design phase.\n\n## Repository Findings\n\n**Current owner of shipment state:** `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-27`\n\n**Current endpoints:**\n- `POST /shipments` (create) - `ShipmentController.kt:26-44`\n- `GET /shipments/{shipmentId}` (read) - `ShipmentController.kt:46-52`\n- `GET /shipments` (list) - `ShipmentController.kt:54-55`\n\n**Error handling infrastructure:**\n- `ResourceNotFoundException` for 404 - `ApiExceptions.kt:19-20`\n- `ConflictException` for 409 - `ApiExceptions.kt:23-24`\n- `ErrorCode` enum - `ApiError.kt:31-37`\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler` - `ApiExceptions.kt:14-28`\n\n**Test infrastructure:**\n- Spring Boot integration tests with MockMvc - `ShipmentControllerTest.kt`\n- 5 existing shipment tests (all passing)\n- Error envelope assertions using `jsonPath(\"$.error.code\")`\n\n## Conventions This Repository Already Has\n\n1. **State-changing endpoints** return `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(saved)` for creation\n2. **Error responses** use a centralized `GlobalExceptionHandler` that wraps all `ApiException` throws into a standard envelope with `error.code`, `message`, and `fields`\n3. **Controllers talk directly to repositories** - no service layer\n4. **Tests verify through separate GET requests** - per the testing-and-verification skill, tests must issue a second GET to verify state was persisted, not just trust the mutating response body\n5. **At least one error case** must assert the `error.code` field, not just the HTTP status\n\n## Affected Files\n\n1. **ShipmentController.kt** — must add `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint\n2. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — must add tests covering all four cases: CREATED→CONFIRMED, CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED (idempotent), CANCELLED rejection, NOT_FOUND rejection\n3. **ApiError.kt** — must add new `ErrorCode` value for state violation (attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment)\n\n## Risks\n\n1. **Idempotency bug**: If the test doesn't verify the second confirm through a separate GET, it won't catch a bug where the second call mutates incorrectly\n2. **State serialization mismatch**: If the response body is assumed correct without a follow-up GET, serialization bugs won't be caught\n3. **Error code consistency**: Must use the new error code only for state violations, not generic 409s\n4. **Concurrent state changes**: The in-memory repository is thread-safe (ConcurrentHashMap), so no risk there\n\n## Open Questions\n\nNone. The ticket defines all four cases clearly: CREATED→CONFIRMED (200), CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED (200, no change), CANCELLED→reject (409), unknown→404.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the `ErrorCode` enum. This code signals that the shipment is in a state incompatible with the confirm operation (e.g., already cancelled). This keeps error semantics precise and allows future state transitions to reuse the same error family.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID, throwing `ResourceNotFoundException` with code `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` if absent (404)\n   - If status is `CREATED`, update to `CONFIRMED`, save, and return 200 with the updated shipment\n   - If status is `CONFIRMED`, return 200 with the current shipment unchanged (idempotent retry)\n   - If status is `CANCELLED`, throw `ConflictException` with code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` (409)\n   - Always return the shipment in the response body\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four new test cases:\n   - `confirms a created shipment` — creates S-X, confirms it, asserts 200 and status=CONFIRMED, then issues a separate GET to verify persistence\n   - `idempotent retry of confirm succeeds` — creates S-X, confirms twice, asserts both return 200 with CONFIRMED, and verifies through GET\n   - `cannot confirm a cancelled shipment` — writes a CANCELLED shipment directly to repository (simulating admin state setup), attempts confirm, asserts 409 with `error.code=SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE`, then issues GET to verify state unchanged\n   - `cannot confirm a nonexistent shipment` — attempts confirm of missing ID, asserts 404 with `error.code=SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n\nI considered placing the confirm logic in a new `ShipmentService` class, but the ticket requires \"The existing Kotlin + Spring Boot architecture must be preserved.\" Since the codebase has no service layer and controllers talk directly to repositories, adding one would violate that constraint. The controller logic is minimal (one conditional on status) and fits the existing pattern.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|-------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| CREATED→CONFIRMED | POST /shipments/S-1/confirm | repository.findById(S-1) | repository.save(updated) | 200, Shipment with CONFIRMED | Return ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) |\n| CONFIRMED idempotent | POST /shipments/S-1/confirm (2nd) | repository.findById(S-1) | none | 200, same Shipment | Return ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) |\n| CANCELLED rejected | POST /shipments/S-cancelled/confirm | repository.findById(S-c) | none | 409, error envelope | throw ConflictException → GlobalExceptionHandler |\n| NOT_FOUND | POST /shipments/missing/confirm | repository.findById(missing) | none | 404, error envelope | throw ResourceNotFoundException → GlobalExceptionHandler |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nEach test follows the testing-and-verification skill pattern:\n\n1. **Test: confirms a created shipment**\n   - Assertion 1: Response body is 200 with status=CONFIRMED ✓ (response body, not just status)\n   - Assertion 2: Separate GET /shipments/S-1, status=CONFIRMED ✓ (second request verifies persistence)\n   - Assertion 3: Second confirm also returns 200 ✓ (exercise the repeat)\n\n2. **Test: idempotent retry succeeds**\n   - First confirm: 200, CONFIRMED\n   - Second confirm: 200, CONFIRMED (same response body)\n   - GET to verify: CONFIRMED (state unchanged)\n\n3. **Test: cannot confirm cancelled shipment**\n   - Setup: repository.save(Shipment(..., CANCELLED))\n   - Attempt confirm: 409, error.code=SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE ✓ (asserts error code)\n   - Verify unchanged: GET shows CANCELLED ✓ (separate GET after refused call)\n\n4. **Test: cannot confirm nonexistent shipment**\n   - Attempt confirm of missing ID: 404, error.code=SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND ✓ (asserts error code)\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the design. Starting with adding the error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1220,"cache_read_input_tokens":22329,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1220},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa8ac858-fc42-4238-8ca1-2e15f2bf0054","uuid":"cf46d37d-717c-464f-a0db-d7b2562273a7","timestamp":"2026-09-09T15:49:09.480Z","request_id":"req_011Cet8RwCerykfjYymt1VcH"}
